# MagiSentry project rule for Windsurf (Cognition)
# Place at: <project>/.windsurf/rules
#
# Windsurf has no native pre-tool hook system. The hard guarantee against
# unscanned installs comes from the universal pip/npm shims (installed by
# `python -m magisentry.setup.install_hooks --tool windsurf`); this rule
# nudges the Windsurf agent to call magisentry directly for cleaner UX.

ALWAYS scan packages before installing them, by invoking the MagiSentry
command-line tool instead of pip/npm/yarn directly:

  - Python:      magisentry pip install <package>
  - JavaScript:  magisentry npm install <package>

NEVER call any of these directly:
  - pip install ...    /  python -m pip install ...
  - npm install ...    /  npm i ...
  - yarn add ...       /  pnpm add ...

If the user provides a `requirements.txt`, run:
  magisentry pip install -r requirements.txt

If MagiSentry reports a THREAT, surface the full output to the user and
WAIT for their decision — do not auto-confirm.
